  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The query is a bicyclic prostaglandin-like free acid (carboxylic acid pKa 4.63, fully ionized at pH 7.4, cyclic hemiacetal/ketone). The most structurally relevant L3 oral-exposure records for prostaglandin analogs show only pg/mL-level systemic exposure after oral dosing: arbaprostil Cmax 91.2 pg/mL (C39), treprostinil AUC0-48 2167 pg·h/mL and Cmin 51.45 pg/mL (C38, C42), and iloprost Cmax 86 pg/mL (C44). This pattern is consistent with extensive first-pass metabolism and low oral bioavailability in this class.",
      "card_ids": ["C38", "C39", "C42", "C44"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 intestinal permeability/solubility records concern acetogenins (annonin-VI, annonacin, squamocin) and imperialine, not the query's prostaglandin-like scaffold; they do not provide query-specific evidence for F >= 20% and do not overturn the low prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C49", "C50", "C51", "C52", "C53", "C54", "C55", "C56", "C57", "C58", "C59", "C60"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L1/L2 high-F analogies (palmitic acid, oxybate, neotame, lefamulin, eplerenone, valomaciclovir stearate, nortilidine, desethyloxybutynin, UDCA, pethidine) are from different chemical classes and are outweighed by the more relevant prostaglandin-analog exposure pattern.",
      "card_ids": ["C16", "C05", "C13", "C18", "C20", "C01", "C02", "C04", "C09", "C06", "C07", "C14", "C21", "C08", "C10", "C03", "C11", "C15", "C12", "C19"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C49", "C50", "C51", "C52", "C53", "C54", "C55", "C56", "C57", "C58", "C59", "C60"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule itself.",
    "L3 oral-exposure records lack IV comparators and complete dose information, so F cannot be computed directly.",
    "L4 permeability/solubility records are for unrelated chemotypes (acetogenins, imperialine, a chroman acid) and do not measure the query's intestinal absorption.",
    "The query's unique hemiacetal, ketone, and gem-difluoride may alter metabolism and absorption in ways not captured by the visible records.",
    "L1/L2 high-F analogies are from different chemical classes and do not provide query-specific endpoint data."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains low: the query is a bicyclic prostaglandin-like free acid, and the most relevant L3 oral-exposure records for prostaglandin analogs show only pg/mL-level systemic exposure after oral dosing, consistent with low oral bioavailability; L4 intestinal permeability/solubility records are for unrelated chemotypes and do not provide query-specific evidence to overturn this. Confidence remains low because no direct F measurement or IV comparator is available."
}

